<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Sugar to tender for 30,000T US soy/corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Sugar to tender for 30,000T US soy/corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Taiwan Sugar Corp will tender on Friday for a combined shipment of 12,000 tonnes of No.2 or better U.S. yellow corn and 18,000 tonnes of No.2 or better U.S. yellow soybeans, traders said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The maximum moisture limits for the shipment are specified as 14.5 percent for the corn and 13.5 percent for the soybeans, traders said.</p>
<p>The tender specifies shipment from the U.S. Gulf or the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>Shipment Tonnage  Date/Location</p>
<p>			 U.S. Gulf	Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> Corn     12,000   Dec 25-Jan 10  Jan 10-25</p>
<p> Soybean  18,000   Dec 25-Jan 10  Jan 10-25</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
